      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T23:22:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like an acceptable amount of noise to me personally. Itemized docs aren\u0027t for reading top-to-bottom, they\u0027re for referencing. Even if the docs are printed all on the same page I don\u0027t feel it would add an unreasonable size to the page.\n\nIf you feel strongly that it\u0027s too much, I would be OK putting a larger disclaimer in fewer places, e.g. `(All docs for this class are AI-generated.)` on all top-level items (classes, enums, whatever) and omit it for things like methods and enum values?",
